    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Opt-in binder\n\nA Telegram bot cannot DM anyone who has not messaged it first, and joining the channel does NOT grant DM permission. This workflow is where DM permission gets captured.\n\n**Flow:** /start -> ask for purchase email -> match against email_norm -> store telegram_chat_id -> reply with their live progress and the channel link.\n\n**SAFETY GATE:** Config.test_mode = true means only chat_ids listed in Config.test_chat_ids get any reply at all. An empty list means nobody gets a reply. To find your own chat_id: message the bot, then read chat_id from the Resolve Bind execution output.\n\n**Bind guards:** max 3 failed email attempts per chat_id; an email already bound to another Telegram account is refused, never rebound.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 1252,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "64d90738-dec2-44d9-9e08-a014d1beccd2",
      "name": "Sticky Note 2b071774",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1616,
        272
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const c = $('Compose Welcome').item.json;\nconst resp = $json || {};\nconst ok = resp.ok === true || Boolean(resp.result && resp.result.message_id);\n\nlet status = 'ok';\nlet err = '';\nif (!ok) {\n  let msg = '';\n  try { msg = String(resp.error || resp.message || JSON.stringify(resp)); } catch (e) { msg = 'unknown error'; }\n  err = msg.slice(0, 300);\n  status = /403|blocked|bot was blocked|chat not found|user is deactivated|deactivated/i.test(msg) ? 'blocked' : 'error';\n}\n\nreturn { json: {\n  row_id: c.row_id,\n  chat_id: c.chat_id,\n  ok: ok,\n  dm_status: status,\n  last_error: err\n}};\n"
      },
